name: Link Analysis audit showcase
tagline: "Procure-to-pay and the journal as a graph - a fictitious vendor, a shell cluster, split invoices, a single point of control, an intercompany round trip, five Demo Users and a Dossier that fails verification when one byte changes"
description: "The Finance and audit Link Analysis showcase as a Space Template (la-audit, vertical B of docs/archived-documents/plans-archive/la-multi-vertical-showcase-plan.md). Five daily-poll Collectors + Pipelines + Datasets of synthetic data (data/inbox): ap_invoice and ap_approval (about 1 800 invoices, 12 months), vendor_master (150), employee_master (60, a tree), gl_journal (40 intercompany journals); the next month waits in data/staged. sql.template Jobs fold them into the link Datasets ap_links (approved, paid_to, reports_to, shares_account, shares_address), its three derived subsets ap_approval_links / ap_identity_links / ap_org_links, gl_links (journal_flow) and ap_duplicate_payments. Planted: vendor V-117 shares bank account and address with employee E-31 and 14 invoices all approved by E-31's manager E-15; five vendors V-131..V-135 on one bank account with a sixth, V-136, deliberately unlinked for Link prediction; 30 invoices 1-3 percent under the 10 000 limit by E-23 to V-099 over six weeks; E-07 signs 70 percent of 20 vendors and is the only bridge into the rest of the approval graph while the org chart is a tree; LE-05 to LE-08 pass 2 400 000 around three quarter ends; 13 duplicate-payment pairs; benign look-alikes the utilities vendor V-001 and the CFO E-01. BASIC TIER (every edition, Basic included): the five feeds and every link Job above, the three saved views, la_index_build (after the ap_links Job) and link-analysis.toon (Entity Types party, marked masked, and legal_entity; the link index ON); masking_mode is left to the edition, so a Basic build, where nobody signs in, shows every id. ADVANCED TIER (a sign-in build; inert on Basic): typed masking of party ids with the admin's audited Reveal, four-eyes above 30, Drafts limits and the committee portal's embed origins (link-analysis.toon, portal/committee-portal.html), la_detect (every 5 minutes; with no Alert Rule bound it evaluates nothing), Demo Users and roles (roles.toon, demo-users.toon: audit.admin, audit.lead, audit.manager, audit.committee, audit.outsider), and the runtime state the seed script writes (tools/seed-la-audit.mjs --apply: Investigations, members, Entity Lists, a Case and a bound Alert Rule); the runbook docs/okf/product/solution-pack/la-audit/admin-guide-showcase-runbook.md needs an Advanced or Preview build with Demo Auth (serve-demo). Synthetic data only; regenerate with tools/gen-la-audit-data.py."
minEdition: basic
icon: heroicons_outline:scale
contents[9]: "5 Pipelines + schemas (feeds landed from data/inbox)", "6 Datasets over the feeds and 6 over the link outputs", "ap_links, 3 derived link Jobs, gl_links and ap_duplicate_payments (sql.template)", "link-analysis.toon (entity types, index ON; typed masking, four-eyes and Drafts on sign-in builds)", "la_index_build Job (after the ap_links Job)", "la_detect Job (cron; Advanced tier, evaluates nothing on Basic)", "3 saved views", "5 Demo Users + role table (Advanced tier, inert on Basic)", "Staged next-month files"
